) are on GND. A0 is therefore tied high.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The specification states the PWM driver I2C address is 0x40, which requires all address pins A0 to A5 to be low (GND).\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"1\\\") (name \\\"+3.3V\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"U2\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"A0\\\") (pintype \\\"input\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The PWM driver answers at address 0x41, not 0x40. The FCC firmware cannot address the servo driver, so servo outputs are not driven as intended.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.45\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"open_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"FCC1\", \"NAVC1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"FCC1.11\", \"FCC1.27\", \"FCC1.50\", \"FCC1.75\", \"FCC1.100\", \"FCC1.14\", \"NAVC1.19\", \"NAVC1.32\", \"NAVC1.48\", \"NAVC1.64\", \"NAVC1.7\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\", \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\", \"unconnected-(FCC1-NRST-Pad14)\", \"unconnected-(NAVC1-NRST-Pad7)\"],\n      \"observed\": \"All VDD pins of FCC1 and NAVC1 (and FCC1 VDDA, VBAT, NRST, and NAVC1 NRST) are on unconnected nets. Only VSS/VSSA is tied to GND, and the 3.3 V rail reaches the NAVC1 only via VBAT.\",\n      \"expected\": \"Every VDD pin of an STM32 must be tied to the 3.3 V rail, and NRST must be wired to the reset net (NRST_FCC / NRST_NAVC, which already carries C31/C49 and the reset switch).\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"216\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"11\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VDD\\\") (pintype \\\"power_in\\\")))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If these are real, the MCUs have no core supply and no reset connection and cannot run. This may be a netlist-export artefact of the reference design rather than a build fault, so the confidence is limited.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The FCC1 VCAP regulator pins are shorted to the UART3 connector nets, which is a clear bridging error. The PCA9685 A0 pin is tied high, which contradicts the specified 0x40 address. The unconnected MCU VDD and NRST pins are a lower-confidence concern.\"\n}",
